#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/nutanix/nutanix.rst:61
msgid ""
"With the above configurations made, click :guilabel:`NEXT`. Choose to add "
"the Cloud to an existing Group or to create a new Group and click "
":guilabel:`NEXT` once again. Finally, review the details of the new Cloud on"
" the REVIEW tab and click :guilabel:`COMPLETE` if all looks good. At this "
"point the new Cloud will be added to |morpheus| and the initial Cloud sync "
"will begin. On the Cloud list page (|InfClo|), we will see the Cloud in an "
"\"OK\" status once it is ready to be consumed in |morpheus| as a "
"provisioning target. Click into the Cloud detail page by clicking on the "
"NAME of the Cloud from the list. Continue on to the next section for an "
"overview of the details available on the Cloud detail."
msgstr ""
"With el anterior configurations made, click :guilabel:`SIGUIENTE`. Choose to"
" add el Cloud to un existente Group o to create un nuevo Group y click "
":guilabel:`SIGUIENTE` once again. Finally, review el detalles of el nuevo "
"Cloud on el REVIEW pestaña y click :guilabel:`COMPLETE` if todos looks good."
" At este point el nuevo Cloud será be agregado to |morpheus| y el initial "
"Cloud sync será begin. En el Cloud página de lista (|InfClo|), we será see "
"el Cloud in un \"OK\" estado once it es ready to be consumed in |morpheus| "
"as un provisioning destino. Click en el Cloud página de detalles by clicking"
" on el NAME of el Cloud desde el lista. Continue on to el siguiente sección "
"para un overview of el detalles disponible on el Cloud detalle."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/nutanix/nutanix.rst:64
msgid "Monitoring Nutanix Clouds"
msgstr "Monitorear Nutanix Clouds"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/nutanix/nutanix.rst:66
msgid ""
"On clicking into the Nutanix Cloud, you'll land on the Summary tab. Here we "
"can see high-level details including cost metrics for the month, general "
"resource utilization information, and information on the number of hosts, "
"workloads, and more that are currently running within the Cloud scope."
msgstr ""
"On clicking en el Nutanix Cloud, you'll land on el Summary pestaña. Here we "
"puede see high-level detalles including cost metrics para el month, general "
"recurso utilization información, y información on el número of hosts, "
"workloads, y más que son actualmente running dentro de el Cloud scope."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/nutanix/nutanix.rst:69
msgid ".. image:: images/integration_guides/clouds/nutanix/cloudDetail.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/integration_guides/clouds/nutanix/cloudDetail.png"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/nutanix/nutanix.rst:70
msgid ""
"You'll also notice the Clusters tab. Here you can see and click into any "
"Docker or Kubernetes Clusters which are running on the Nutanix Cloud. "
"|morpheus| will see these clusters as provisioning targets themselves for "
"containerized applications (as opposed to the Cloud itself for virtualized "
"applications). You can also add new Kubernetes or Dockers clusters from this"
" tab. |morpheus| includes built-in Cluster Layouts but custom Cluster "
"Layouts can also be created. There is a guide on creating your own custom "
"Kubernetes Cluster Layouts in the Clusters section of |morpheus| UI "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"You'll también notice el Clusters pestaña. Here you puede see y click en "
"cualquier Docker o Kubernetes Clusters cual son running on el Nutanix Cloud."
" |morpheus| será see estos clusters as provisioning targets themselves para "
"containerized applications (as opposed to el Cloud itself para virtualized "
"applications). You puede también add nuevo Kubernetes o Dockers clusters "
"desde este pestaña. |morpheus| includes built-in Cluster Layouts pero "
"personalizado Cluster Layouts puede también be creado. There es un guía on "
"creating your own personalizado Kubernetes Cluster Layouts in el Clusters "
"sección of |morpheus| UI documentación."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/nutanix/nutanix.rst:72
msgid ""
"On the Hosts tab, you'll see all Nutanix hypervisior hosts which are "
"associated with the cluster. Host health metrics are viewable and we can "
"click into individual hosts to see even greater detail on the individual "
"host detail pages."
msgstr ""
"En el Hosts pestaña, you'll see todos Nutanix hypervisior hosts cual son "
"asociado con el clúster. Host health metrics son viewable y we puede click "
"en individual hosts to see incluso greater detalle on el individual host "
"página de detalless."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/nutanix/nutanix.rst:74
msgid ""
"The VM and Containers tabs show all current VM and container workloads "
"across the cluster. When integrating the Cloud, if you opted to inventory "
"existing workloads, discovered resources will appear here. If not (or if "
"there simply are none), only |morpheus|-provisioned workloads will appear "
"here."
msgstr ""
"The VM y Containers tabs show todos actual VM y container workloads across "
"el clúster. When integrating el Cloud, if you opted to inventory existente "
"workloads, discovered recursos será appear aquí. If no (o if allí simply son"
" none), solo |morpheus|-provisioned workloads será appear aquí."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/nutanix/nutanix.rst:77
msgid "Provisioning New Workloads"
msgstr "Aprovisionar New Workloads"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/nutanix/nutanix.rst:79
msgid ""
"With the Cloud integrated, you're already to provision new workloads. "
"|morpheus| comes pre-installed with a number of default library items "
"designed to work with each supported Cloud integration type, including "
"Nutanix. While this guide will not go through the process of using the "
"provisioning wizard (see |ProIns| page to start), you could provision a "
"default workload to test functionality now if desired. Additionally, "
"|morpheus| will sync Virtual Images from Nutanix Clouds (|LibVir|) and "
"custom Library items may be built from these images. See the Library section"
" of |morpheus| documentation for more information on piecing together "
"Instance Types, images, and automation scripts into cohesive and easily-"
"consumed Library items."
msgstr ""
"With el Cloud integrated, you're ya to provision nuevo workloads. |morpheus|"
" comes pre-instalado con un número of predeterminado library elementos "
"designed to work con cada compatible Cloud integration tipo, including "
"Nutanix. While este guía no go a través de el proceso of using el "
"provisioning wizard (see |ProIns| página to start), you podría provision un "
"predeterminado workload to test functionality ahora si se desea. "
"Adicionalmente, |morpheus| será sync Virtual Images desde Nutanix Clouds "
"(|LibVir|) y personalizado Library elementos puede be built desde estos "
"images. See el Library sección of |morpheus| documentación para más "
"información on piecing together Instance Types, images, y automation scripts"
" en cohesive y easily-consumed Library elementos."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/nutanix/nutanix.rst:84
msgid ""
"|morpheus| includes a default set of Service Plans. These Service Plans can "
"be considered akin to AWS Flavors or Openstack Flavors. They provide a means"
" to set predefined tiers on memory, storage, and CPU cores. Price tables can"
" also be applied to these so estimated cost per virtual machine can be "
"tracked as well as pricing for customers. By default, these options are "
"fixed sizes but can be configured for dynamic sizing. A service plan can be "
"configured to allow a custom user entry for memory, storage, or cpu. To "
"configure this, simply edit an existing Service Plan tied to Nutanix or "
"create a new one. These all can be easily managed from the |AdmPla| section."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| includes un predeterminado set of Service Plans. These Service "
"Plans puede be considered akin to AWS Flavors o Openstack Flavors. They "
"provide un means to set predefined tiers on memory, storage, y CPU cores. "
"Price tables puede también be applied to estos so estimated cost per virtual"
" machine puede be tracked así como pricing para customers. By "
"predeterminado, estos opciones son fixed sizes pero se puede configurar para"
" dynamic sizing. A servicio plan se puede configurar to allow un "
"personalizado user entry para memory, storage, o cpu. To configure este, "
"simply edit un existente Service Plan tied to Nutanix o create un nuevo one."
" These todos puede be easily managed desde el |AdmPla| sección."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/nutanix/nutanix.rst:87
msgid "Docker"
msgstr "Docker"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/nutanix/nutanix.rst:89
msgid ""
"So far, this document has covered how to add the Nutanix cloud integration "
"and has enabled users the ability to provision virtual machine-based "
"Instances. Another great feature provided by |morpheus| out of the box is "
"the ability to use Docker containers and even support multiple containers "
"per Docker host. To do this, a Docker Host must first be provisioned into "
"Nutanix (multiple are needed when dealing with horizontal scaling "
"scenarios). As mentioned previously, these can be viewed or created from the"
" Clusters tab of the Cloud detail page."
msgstr ""
"So far, este document tiene covered how to add el Nutanix cloud integration "
"y tiene habilitado users el ability to provision virtual machine-based "
"Instances. Another great característica provided by |morpheus| out of el box"
" es el ability to use Docker containers y incluso support múltiples "
"containers per Docker host. To do este, un Docker Host debe primero be "
"provisioned en Nutanix (múltiples son needed cuando dealing con horizontal "
"scaling scenarios). As mentioned previamente, estos se puede ver o creado "
"desde el Clusters pestaña of el Cloud página de detalles."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/nutanix/nutanix.rst:91
msgid ""
"To provision a Docker Host, simply navigate to the Cloud detail page or "
"|InfClu| section. From there, click :guilabel:`+ ADD CLUSTER` to add a "
"Nutanix Docker Host. |morpheus| views a Docker host just like any other "
"Hypervisor with the caveat being that it is used for running containerized "
"images instead of virtualized ones. Once a Docker Host is successfully "
"provisioned, a green checkmark will appear to the right of the host marking "
"it as available for use. In the event of a failure, click into the relevant "
"host that failed and an error explaining the failure will be displayed in "
"red at the top. Just like with VMs, |morpheus| includes default "
"containerized items out of the box so provisioning to Docker hosts can be "
"tested even before you've created your own container-based Library items."
msgstr ""
"To provision un Docker Host, simply navigate to el Cloud página de detalles "
"o |InfClu| sección. Desde elre, click :guilabel:`+ AGREGAR CLUSTER` to add "
"un Nutanix Docker Host. |morpheus| views un Docker host solo like cualquier "
"otro Hypervisor con el caveat being que it se utiliza para running "
"containerized images en cambio of virtualized ones. Once un Docker Host es "
"successfully provisioned, un green checkmark será appear to el right of el "
"host marking it as disponible para use. En el evento of un failure, click en"
" el relevante host que fallido y un error explaining el failure se mostrará "
"in red en la parte superior. Just like con VMs, |morpheus| includes "
"predeterminado containerized elementos out of el box so provisioning to "
"Docker hosts puede be tested incluso antes de you've creado your own "
"container-based Library elementos."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/nutanix/nutanix.rst:93
msgid ""
"Some common error scenarios include network connectivity. For a Docker Host "
"to function properly, it must be able to resolve the |morpheus| appliance "
"URL which can be configured in |AdmSet|. If it is unable to resolve and "
"negotiate with the appliance, then the Agent installation will fail and "
"provisioning instructions will not be able to be issued to the host."
msgstr ""
"Some common error scenarios include network connectivity. For un Docker Host"
" to función properly, it debe be able to resolve el |morpheus| appliance URL"
" cual se puede configurar in |AdmSet|. If it es unable to resolve y "
"negotiate con el appliance, entonces el Agent instalación será fail y "
"provisioning instructions no be able to be issued to el host."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/nutanix/nutanix.rst:96
msgid "Snapshots"
msgstr "Snapshots"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/nutanix/nutanix.rst:98
msgid ""
"|morpheus| allows the ability to create a snapshot of a Nutanix Instance.  "
"From the Instance detail page, simply select ``Actions > Create Snapshot`` "
"to begin creation of a new Snapshot. Existing snapshots can be viewed in the"
" ``BACKUPS`` tab on the Instance detail page. Snapshots taken outside "
"|morpheus| will be synced every five minutes (by default). To revert to a "
"previous snapshot, click on the revert icon located on the right side of the"
" Snapshot. Snapshots can be deleted by clicking on the trash can icon."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| allows el ability to create un snapshot of un Nutanix Instance.  "
"Desde el Instance página de detalles, simply select ``Actions > Create "
"Snapshot`` to begin creation of un nuevo Snapshot. Existing snapshots se "
"puede ver in el ``BACKUPS`` pestaña on el Instance página de detalles. "
"Snapshots taken outside |morpheus| será be synced cada five minutes (por "
"defecto). To revert to un anterior snapshot, click on el revert icon located"
" un la derecha side of el Snapshot. Snapshots se puede eliminar by clicking "
"on el trash puede icon."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/nutanix/nutanix.rst:100
msgid ""
"Access to Snapshots can be limited or removed entirely for specific user "
"roles as needed. To edit a role's Snapshots permissions, go to |AdmRol| > "
"(Your selected role) > Snapshots. Users can be given Full, Read-only, or No "
"access."
msgstr ""
"Access to Snapshots puede be limited o eliminado entirely para específico "
"user roles según sea necesario. To edit un rol's Snapshots permisos, go to "
"|AdmRol| > (Your seleccionado role) > Snapshots. Users puede be given Full, "
"Read-solo, o No acceso."
